# .disclose-allow — exemptions for THIS repository's own fixtures, read by the shared disclose
# workflow from the pull request's BASE (so a pull request cannot widen the exemptions that judge
# it). One per line: <rule-glob> <location-glob> <reason of three words or more>. A location glob
# covers a tree path and the same path inside a built tarball. See `devkit disclose --help`.
#
# Nothing is exempted: the gate's own suite assembles every planted value at run time, so no file
# here carries one. In particular no generic `mac` line exists — a fixture MAC is locally
# administered (the second-lowest bit of its first octet set) and needs no exemption.
